body:
Thanks for reporting! I can reproduce the issue.

My initial investigation shows that playback is stuck in a buffering state because the loading thread is indefinitely blocked on `timestampAdjuster.waitUntilInitialized()` in `HlsMediaChunk`.  Note that this only happens when you try to play past the discontinuity. For example seeking to a later position in the stream works just fine. Not sure if this is because the media is somehow broken or whether this is a bug in ExoPlayer. But even for broken media, we shouldn't end up blocking forever without an error. 

@christosts  Do you want to take a look because it's an HLS issue?
